  "description": "\u201cIf a parallelogram have the same base with a triangle and be in the same parallels, the parallelogram is double of the triangle.\u201d\n\u2014 Euclid's Elements, BOOK I \u2022 PROP. 41 (G.70)\n\n00:00 1 \u00b7 GIVEN: \u27e8 A B C D \u27e9, \u27e8 E B C \u27e9 (/ B C / \u2225 / A E /)\n00:23 2 \u00b7 CONSTRUCT: segment(A, C) \u2192 / A C /\n00:31 3 \u00b7 ASSERT: / B C / \u2225 / A E / \u2192 \u27e8 A B C \u27e9 = \u27e8 E B C \u27e9\n00:41 4 \u00b7 ASSERT: / A C / \u2208 \u27e8 A B C D \u27e9 \u2192 \u27e8 A B C D \u27e9 = 2 \u27e8 A B C \u27e9\n00:51 5 \u00b7 \u2234: \u27e8 A B C D \u27e9 = 2 \u27e8 A B C \u27e9, \u27e8 A B C \u27e9 = \u27e8 E B C \u27e9 \u2192 \u27e8 A B C D \u27e9 = 2 \u27e8 E B C \u27e9\n\nGEOMETOR \u2022 G.70 \u2022 v2",
